recommendation:
Add a nonReentrant modifier (from OpenZeppelin ReentrancyGuard) to depositUnderlying and withdrawUnderlying. Also follow checks-effects-interactions: perform state changes (mint/burn) before external calls. Since _afterTokenTransfer is called inside _mint/_burn, consider restructuring to use _beforeTokenTransfer instead, or accept the ordering issue and rely on reentrancy guard. Example:

import {ReentrancyGuard} from '@openzeppelin/contracts/security/ReentrancyGuard.sol';
contract LiquidityGauge is ERC20, ERC20Burnable, ReentrancyGuard {
    function depositUnderlying(uint256 _amount) external nonReentrant { ... }
    function withdrawUnderlying(uint256 _amount) external nonReentrant { ... }
}
